NAME
       diff - compare files line by line

SYNOPSIS
       diff [-abBiNqrsTwZ] [-u | -U N | -c | -C N | -e |
          --normal] [--label L] [--strip-trailing-cr] [-x PAT]
          [--minimal] file1 file2

DESCRIPTION
       Compare files line by line. Exit status: 0 same, 1
       different, 2 trouble.  The edit script comes from
       Myers' O(ND) algorithm in its linear-space form: find
       the middle snake of an optimal path from both ends at
       once, then solve the two halves the same way. Runs of
       changes are then slid as far towards the end as the
       text allows, as GNU diff does, so ambiguous changes are
       reported in the same place. When the edit distance gets
       very large (two mostly different big files) the search
       stops early and splits at the furthest point reached,
       which keeps the time bounded but may report a longer
       script than the shortest one; --minimal turns that off.

NOTES
       Long comparisons yield to the kernel every million
       steps, so the system stays responsive.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

